DESCRIPTION:What you’ll doIn this 4-session course\, students will be in
 troduced to hand sewing and weaving through several projects. Historical c
 ontext will be given with each activity starting with ancient origins\, fo
 llowed by the tools of these crafts and how they have evolved\, cultural s
 ignificance of patterns. We will wrap up with the journey of textiles thro
 ugh history. All supplies are provided and students will take home all of 
 their projects and handouts.Membership has its benefitsAllSilver Membersh
LOCATION:Room 116\, 276 East Napa Street\, Sonoma\, CA
