SUMMARY: Winsor & Newton Professional Watercolour Series - Class 1 of 3: 
 Abstract Stones
DESCRIPTION:Instructor: Ryan Martin\n\nDate: Monday\, November 2nd\n\nTim
 e: 12:30PM-2PM\n\nLocation: Santa Rosa Store\n\nFree!\n\n\nClass 1 of 3: 
 Abstract Stones. This is number one in a series of three classes using Wi
 nsor & Newton Professional Watercolour with artist Ryan Martin. Attend al
 l three to learn week-by-week from Ryan but none are prerequisites if you
 r schedule does not allow. Ryan will guide you through creating organic “
 stones” using Winsor & Newton Professional Watercolours and Art Masking F
 luid to preserve bright highlights and add texture. You’ll experiment wit
 h wet-into-wet techniques\, learn the attributes of different pigments\, 
 how they bloom or granulate differently\, and experiment using masking fl
 uid to create veins\, cracks\, and white accents. No drawing experience i
 s needed\; this class is all about letting the water and the pigment do t
 he work! It’s a hands-on\, fun way to explore how color\, texture\, and p
 rocess come together to create beautiful\, abstract compositions. All sup
 plies are provided\, so you can try different pigments\, colors\, and bru
 shes and discover what you enjoy using. Ryan will also be available after
  class to answer questions and help you choose materials to keep explorin
 g at home.\n\nLimited seats available—reserve your spot today!\n\n\nRyan 
 Martin lives and works in the San Francisco Bay Area where he attended th
 e California College of the Arts. Through painting and drawing\, Martin c
 reates surreal\, dream-like compositions of his subjects. He is influence
 d by his Native American (Mexican/Seri) and Russian heritage through pain
 ting reinterpretations of war bonnets and kokoshniks haloing his subjects
 . Martin’s artwork has been highlighted by numerous media including The A
 dvocate\, Creative Boom\, The Art of Man and others. He has exhibited wid
 ely across the United States\, including the deYoung Museum\, Mark Wolfe 
 Contemporary\, Modern Eden Gallery of San Francisco\, Elizabeth Houston G
 allery of NYC\, as well as numerous fairs including SCOPE\, Untitled Art 
 in Miami and Volta NY.\n\nWebsite: ryanmartinart.com http://ryanmartinart
 .com • Instagram: @ryanmartinart
CATEGORIES:Santa-Rosa,Watercolor,Free-Demo
X-TKF-FEATURED-IMAGE:https://d3flpus5evl89n.cloudfront.net/640bcf85795edf
 4fa3769ae5/6ad8157462b7c5607cfc1664/scaled_768.jpg
X-TKF-CUSTOM-PREVIEW:Instructor: Ryan Martin Date: Monday\, November 2nd 
 Time: 12:30PM-2PM Location: Santa Rosa Store Free! Class 1 of 3: Abstract
  Stones. This is number one in a...
LOCATION:Rileystreet Art Supply\,103 Maxwell Ct\, Santa Rosa\, CA 95401\,
  USA
CREATED:20261021T014407Z
