 mmunity with residents of Sonoma County to screen and discuss significant 
 classic and modern cinema. Within the series\, our Filmmakers in Conversat
 ion program regularly hosts directors\, actors\, and motion picture techni
 cians.</p><p>  Guest evenings are <em>generally</em> structured with a 6pm
  talk or filmmaker interview\, a 7pm screening\, and a question &amp\; ans
 wer session following the film.</p><p>  The program is hosted in the Carol
 e L. Ellis Auditorium on the SRJC Petaluma Campus. Films are projected in 
