X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Sebastopol Center for the Arts": "https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/art-as-self-discovery-mixed-media-art-1"}
X-SOURCE-ID:sebarts
SUMMARY:Art as Self Discovery: Mixed Media Art  — Sebastopol Center For 
 the Arts\, California
DTSTART:20261105T000000
DTEND:20261106T000000
UID:f56be7a5629329345a3d2f57b2067a3e@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Art as Self-Discovery: Mixed Media Art (November 2026)\n\n  \n
     \n      \n        \n          $287.00\n        \n      \n    \n  \n\nA
 rt as Self-Discovery: Mixed Media Art Every-Other Thursday\, 5:30-8:30pm\,
  November 5th\,  19th\, December 3rd\, and 17thAttendance: $275.00 + $12.0
 0 Materials Fee Class Description: In this 4 session series\, students wil
 l explore the art of creating mixed-media art with multiple techniques. Ma
 rion will guide you through the basics of composition\, color theory\, and
  image selection. This workshop is designed for people of all creative lev
 els who wish to learn collage and mixed media skills\, connect with the co
 mmunity\, and engage in meaningful self-expression. Students will have ac
 cess to a curated selection of collage materials\, paints\, and scissors\,
  and are encouraged to bring magazines and personal images of choice. We w
 ill explore image selection and composition\, layering and embedding 3D ob
 jects\, as well as choosing mounting surfaces and framing. Marion will off
 er individual and group guidance in each class. While we’ll appreciate 
 the aesthetic aspects of the work\, we will focus on the personal meaning 
 and process for each piece. This is a space for connection and non-judgeme
 nt\, where your unique creative expression matters above all - inviting cu
 riosity and play to reveal new pathways of seeing and creating. Students 
 are encouraged to bring the following materials: Gloves Preferred Glue 
 Preferred scissorsAbout the Teacher: Marion Ruta Segal has been a practici
 ng mixed media artist with nearly 20 years of teaching experience in New Y
 ork City and the San Francisco Bay Area. Her work has been exhibited publi
 cly since 2013. Marion has taught at community organizations and at the co
 llege level\, leading workshops that invite students into exploratory\, me
 aning-focused making - grounding them in core methods and aesthetics inclu
 ding design\, color theory\, and composition. She brings warmth\, depth\, 
 and care to the studio\, meeting participants wherever they are at creativ
 ely. Click here to learn more about Marion! \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\
 n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n          \n            \n           
    \n                Add to cart
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts\, 282 S High St\, Sebastopol\, CA 
 95472
URL:https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/art-as-self-discovery-mixed-m
 edia-art-1
X-SOURCE:Sebastopol Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Sebastopol Center for the Arts": "https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/holiday-handbuilding-3-sessions"}
X-SOURCE-ID:sebarts
SUMMARY:Holiday Handbuilding (3 sessions)  — Sebastopol Center For the A
 rts\, California
DTSTART:20261105T000000
DTEND:20261106T000000
UID:50f937f248237d278ac924c615cb731a@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Holiday Handbuilding\n\n  \n    \n      \n        \n          
 $135.00\n        \n      \n    \n  \n\nHoliday Handbuilding Thursdays\, No
 vember 5th\, 12th\, and 19th from 6:00-9:00pm $90.00 Attendance Price + $4
 5.00 Clay Fee = $135.00Maximum of 10 students. Class Description: Get read
 y to deck your halls with handmade charm! Join us for our Holiday Handbuil
 ding Class\, where you will create some holiday themed pieces for the seas
 on of giving using and refining techniques you’ve already tried. In this
  festive workshop\, you will craft your own seasonal treasures\, from cust
 omer ornaments and cozy mugs to unique holiday decor and heartfelt gifts -
  with your hands!  Michael will guide you through numerous demonstrations 
 to help you bring your creative visions to life. Grab a friend\, embrace t
 he holiday spirit\, and build pieces that will become part of your holiday
  tradition!About the Instructor: Michael Citrino has had a love affair wit
 h clay for over 50 years. After his college experience at California Colle
 ge of Arts and Crafts with Viola Frey and further work at Humboldt State U
 niversity with Lew Merrick\, he ran a stained glass business for 18 years.
  Michael and his wife left for Turkey in 1991 to teach in International Sc
 hools. For 26 years he taught K-12 art\, including Ceramics\, Drawing\, Ph
 otography\, Design and Sculpture at schools in six different countries. He
  started clay programs for High School and Middle School students at three
  of those schools. At four of these schools he offered after school and we
 ekend ceramics sessions for teachers and parents. Michael’s work ranges 
 from the traditional to the experimental and a wide swath in between. His 
 approach to teaching is to help students explore the playful nature of the
  clay room and nurture a love for the possibilities that medium presents.\
 n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n         
  \n            \n              \n                Add to cart
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts\, 282 S High St\, Sebastopol\, CA 
 95472
URL:https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/holiday-handbuilding-3-sessio
 ns
X-SOURCE:Sebastopol Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
