CATEGORIES:Department Events
DESCRIPTION:Learn how to recognize the warning signs of suicide\, start a 
 supportive conversation\, and connect someone to help.  QPR (Question\, Pe
 rsuade\, Refer) is a suicide prevention training that gives you practical 
 skills to recognize when someone may be struggling and take action. Whethe
 r you're interested in mental health\, supporting friends and peers\, or s
 imply want to be better prepared to help someone in need\, this training c
 an help you feel more confident responding to a crisis.  In this training\
 , you'll learn how to:Recognize warning signs and risk factors  Identify w
 hen someone may be experiencing a mental health crisis  Ask about suicide 
 in a direct and supportive way  Connect someone with appropriate help and 
 resources  Use the QPR approach to support someone in need  To register vi
 sit the Student Health Services website. (https://shs.santarosa.edu/11-5-2
 6-qpr)
LAST-MODIFIED:20260903T214938Z
LOCATION:Student Health Services\, Bertolini Student Center - Santa Rosa C
 ampus
URL:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/event/23962-qpr-question-persuade-refer
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Learn how to recognize the warning signs
  of suicide\, start a supportive conversation\, and connect someone to hel
 p.</p><p>  QPR (Question\, Persuade\, Refer) is a suicide prevention train
 ing that gives you practical skills to recognize when someone may be strug
 gling and take action. Whether you're interested in mental health\, suppor
 ting friends and peers\, or simply want to be better prepared to help some
 one in need\, this training can help you feel more confident responding to
  a crisis.</p><p>  In this training\, you'll learn how to:</p><ul><li>Reco
 gnize warning signs and risk factors  </li><li>Identify when someone may b
 e experiencing a mental health crisis  </li><li>Ask about suicide in a dir
 ect and supportive way  </li><li>Connect someone with appropriate help and
  resources  </li><li>Use the QPR approach to support someone in need  </li
 ></ul><p><a href="https://shs.santarosa.edu/11-5-26-qpr" target="_blank" r
 el="noopener">To register visit the Student Health Services website.</a></
 p>
