DESCRIPTION:As generative AI becomes embedded across disciplines\, higher 
 education faces a pivotal moment—not of battle between opposing camps\, 
 but of intentional design.  Generative systems offer novel capabilities fo
 r research\, creation\, and learning\, yet their ultimate value depends en
 tirely on how thoughtfully we guide them.Nick Fitzpatrick is an SRJC alum 
 and during his graduate studies he interned at Geopogo\, a startup at the 
 intersection of artificial intelligence and architecture\, building AI des
 ign and code-compliance tools that automate workflows for architecture fir
 ms.Learn more on the SRJC Computer Studies' AI Talks website. (https://cs.
 santarosa.edu/ai-talks-2026)
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T190519Z
LOCATION:Online
URL:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/event/23945-nick-fitzpatrick-human-agen
 cy-machine-inquiry
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  As generative AI becomes embedded across
  disciplines\, higher education faces a pivotal moment—not of battle bet
 ween opposing camps\, but of intentional design.</p><p>  Generative system
 s offer novel capabilities for research\, creation\, and learning\, yet th
 eir ultimate value depends entirely on how thoughtfully we guide them.</p>
 <p><strong>Nick Fitzpatrick</strong> is an SRJC alum and during his gradua
 te studies he interned at Geopogo\, a startup at the intersection of artif
 icial intelligence and architecture\, building AI design and code-complian
 ce tools that automate workflows for architecture firms.</p><p><a href="ht
 tps://cs.santarosa.edu/ai-talks-2026" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Learn
  more on the SRJC Computer Studies' AI Talks website.</a></p>
