SUMMARY:Mercy Presents: Last Mic Standing Comedy Showdown
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261106T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261106T220000
UID:260701aDCBsJYQSEuuU4lZav6MkA
DESCRIPTION:Battle for the Main Stage.\n\nEight fearless comics step into 
 the spotlight for one night of rapid-fire punchlines\, crowd reactions\, a
 nd high-stakes humor inside The Lounge at Mercy.\n\nThis isn’t an open m
 ic. This is a showdown.\n\n8 Comics. 3 Judges. Audience Vote.\n\nEach come
 dian brings their sharpest material and strongest stage presence to compet
 e for the title of Last Mic Standing. Judges score the sets. The crowd wei
 ghs in. The energy decides everything.\n\nOne night. One winner.\n\nThe st
 akes are real. The winner takes home a $100 cash prize and earns a paid ho
 sting spot at the next Mercy’s Tokes & Jokes Comedy Night. Win the crowd
 . Own the mic. Come back as host.\n\nThis is a 420-friendly comedy competi
 tion hosted inside our fully licensed cannabis consumption lounge\, where 
 elevated vibes meet elevated punchlines. Guests are welcome to enjoy respo
 nsibly while comics go head-to-head under the lights. Great sets hit diffe
 rently here.\n\nDate & Time\n\nDate: First Friday of Every Month\n\nTime: 
 8:00 PM – 9:30 PM\n\nDoors Open: 6:00 PM\n\nTicket Tiers\n\n$20 — Gene
 ral Admission \\(Open Seating\\) Entry to Comedy Showdown 🎤 Open seatin
 g \\(first come\, first served\\). Come early for the best spot.\n\n$30 
 — GA \\+ Goodie Bag A little extra ✨ Entry \\+ goodie bag \\($15 value
 \\) included. Open seating \\(first come\, first served\\). \n\n⭐ $40 
 — Preferred Bucket Seat \\+ Goodie Bag \\(Most Popular\\) Comfort upgrad
 e ⭐ Guaranteed bucket seat \\+ shared table access\, plus goodie bag \\(
 $15 value\\) included. Limited seating.\n\n🔥 $135 — Couch Crew Pass \
 \(3 Guests \\+ Premium Bag\\) Bring your crew 🔥 Includes admission for 
 3 guests\, reserved couch seating with a dedicated table\, plus premium ba
 g \\($100 value\\) included. Only 11 couches.\n\n21\\+ Only | DCC \\# C12-
 0000420-LIC\n\nEvent Terms & Conditions\n\nThis event is 21\\+ only. Valid
  government-issued ID is required for entry. By attending this event at th
 e Mercy Wellness Lounge\, you acknowledge that photography and video recor
 ding may take place. Images and footage may be used by Mercy Wellness for 
 marketing and promotional purposes across various channels\, without compe
 nsation. Tickets are non-refundable unless otherwise stated. Event details
 \, timing\, or programming are subject to change.\n\nCannabis consumption 
 is limited to designated areas and must comply with all applicable local a
 nd state regulations. Please consume responsibly.\n\nBy entering the venue
 \, you agree to comply with all house rules and venue policies.
LOCATION:The Lounge at Mercy
URL:https://mercywellness.com/tokes-n-jokes-comedy-night
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Occidental Center for the Arts": "https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/electric-tumbleweed-3", "Creative Sonoma": "https://creativesonoma.org/event/electric-tumbleweed/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Occidental Center for the Arts": "https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/electric-tumbleweed-3"}
X-SOURCE-ID:occidental_arts
SUMMARY:Electric Tumbleweed
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261106T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261106T230000
UID:6a8cd14063ff376f3d80db4a@squarespace.com
DESCRIPTION:Occidental Center for the Arts presents Electric Tumbleweed! O
 ne of Sonoma County's finest bands returns for our listening and dancing p
 leasure.\nTickets are $20/$15 for OCA members. Doors open at 7:30 PM. No d
 ogs. Refreshments available. Free parking.\nGet Tickets\nElectric Tumblewe
 ed is a psychedelic outlaw country group based in Sonoma County\, Californ
 ia. Founded in 2019 by members rooted in bluegrass\, country\, and psyched
 elic rock\, the music is a hard driving mixture of twangy guitar and psych
 edelic noise\, held together by a steady rhythm section with the cry of pe
 dal steel layered in between it all. Electric Tumbleweed has maintained st
 eady momentum in the Northern California music scene\; backing David Nelso
 n (New Riders of the Purple Sage) on multiple occasions\; most notably at 
 the Mystic Theater with guest Mark Karan (Ratdog) for a sold out performan
 ce. Electric Tumbleweed performed regularly at Phil Lesh’s Terrapin Cros
 sroads as a solo group as well as with Scott Law\, Barry Sless (Phil Lesh 
 and Friends) and Dave Zirbel (Sammy Hagar Band) are regular pedal steel pl
 ayers in the group. The band has been invited to play multiple festivals a
 nd events including The String Cheese Incident’s Hog Farm Hideaway\, Ain
 ’t Necessarily Dead Fest (backing David Nelson). We aim to keep our goal
 s high\, and to perform high quality music\; focusing on writing and arran
 ging new songs\, and booking future tour dates. We are excited to release 
 our debut full-length album in October 2021\, which features Sam Bush (New
  Grass Revival)\, Barry Sless (Phil Lesh & Friends)\, and Lester and Dylan
  Chambers (The Chambers Brothers). The album features the artwork of Stanl
 ey Mouse/Jennae Bennett and was engineered and mastered by Grammy winning 
 Oz Fritz (Tom Waits).
LOCATION:Occidental Center for the Arts\, 3850 Doris Murphy Court\, Occide
 ntal\, CA 95465
URL:https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/electric-tu
 mbleweed-3
X-SOURCE:Occidental Center for the Arts, Creative Sonoma
END:VEVENT
