SUMMARY:Free Park Admission for Veterans and Active Military
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T170000
UID:261028bdeqzwTfGUaya8LmvrbIJQ
DESCRIPTION:In recognition of their service to the United States\, Jack Lo
 ndon State Historic Park will provide free admission to all active-duty mi
 litary and veterans on Nov. 7\, 8\, 9\, 10\, and 11 - Veterans Day – 202
 6.\n\nBlending the fascinating history of one of America’s most prolific
  and successful writers with the serenity of nature\, Jack London State Hi
 storic Park offers more than 29 miles of back-country trails that roam thr
 ough mixed forests\, redwood groves\, oak woodlands\, and grassy meadows i
 n Sonoma County’s Valley of the Moon.  \n\nActive duty or retired mili
 tary identification or form DD214 can be presented at the entry kiosk to r
 eceive free admission.\n\nAdmission\, regularly priced at $15\, covers one
  vehicle of up to nine passengers for the day.  Park hours are 9 a.m. to 
 5 p.m. daily.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park - Oak Grove Picnic Area (standing
  capacity)
URL:http://www.jacklondonpark.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://solanolandtrust.org/events-news/event-calendar.html/event/2026/11/07/nature-hike-at-vallejo-swett-ranches-november-/573999"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Nature Hike at Vallejo Swett-Ranches
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T130000
UID:261027qJU8AXYGoke35WrOC6EU-g
DESCRIPTION:Come explore the hills between Fairfield\, Benicia\, and Valle
 jo. Solano Land Trust docents will guide you through this area\, known as 
 the King-Swett Ranches. Docents will share insights about the birds and ot
 her wildlife that call this area home\, and give you a great workout!\n\nH
 ike level: Moderate to Moderately Strenuous. Please note: Vallejo Swett is
  an undeveloped property with no formal trails. This is a rugged & an off 
 trail hike. Participants could be climbing or going under fences\, and tre
 e branches. Docents also can go up & along of steep and clumpy ground moun
 tain sides.\n\n\\*Please note\, cancellation of the hike may occur due to 
 County Fire Danger Warnings and closures of open spaces and parks. Once re
 gistered\, you will receive any updates should this ever happen.
LOCATION:King-Swett Ranches
URL:https://solanolandtrust.org/events-news/event-calendar.html/event/2026
 /11/07/nature-hike-at-vallejo-swett-ranches-november-/573999
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
