DESCRIPTION:Join Jack London Park Partners and Sonoma Ecology Center staff
  in a series of intermediate hikes\, guided in Spanish\, between Jack Lond
 on State Historic Park and Sugarloaf Ridge State Park. Each hike is a roun
 d trip\, returning to the starting point\, and will increase in length or 
 difficulty. Not appropriate for children under 12 years old.\n\nSat. Nov. 
 7 – Gunsight Rock at Sugarloaf/Hood Mountain Regional Park. 6.44 miles\,
  2\,129 ft. elevation (meet at Sugarloaf Ridge State Park).\n\nSun. Nov. 1
 5 – Sonoma Ridge in Sonoma Developmental Center/Jack London. 9.67 miles\
 , 2\,126 ft. elevation (meet at the intersection of Arnold Dr. and Harney 
 Rd.\, inside the SDC).\n\nSat.  Nov. 21 – "The Big Loop" at Sugarloaf. 
 7.37 miles\, 1\,739 ft elevation (meet at Sugarloaf Ridge State Park).
