BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Occidental Center for the Arts": "https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/dublinesque-album-release-party", "North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/dublinesque-album-release-party", "Creative Sonoma": "https://creativesonoma.org/event/dublinesque-album-release-party/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Occidental Center for the Arts": "https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/dublinesque-album-release-party"}
X-SOURCE-ID:occidental_arts
SUMMARY:Dublinesque Album Release Party
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T210000
UID:6a8ceb1a76585f118aa96edc@squarespace.com
DESCRIPTION:Don't miss this special evening where we’ll take a musical t
 rip to Dublin with some of the Bay Area’s finest musicians and singers! 
 Eamonn Flynn\, Darcy Noonan\, Hector Bragado and Felim Egan will dazzle us
  with their traditional and original "Dublinesque" harmonies. OCA favorite
 s through and through\, we're just delighted to bring back this spirited\,
  talented group.\nTickets are $25\, $20 for OCA members. Doors open at 6:3
 0 PM. Refreshments available\, art gallery open during intermission.\nGet 
 Tickets\nEAMONN FLYNN & DUBLINESQUE\nEamonn Flynn forges his own brand of 
 Irish soul. The Dublin-born singer-songwriter/pianist got his start with T
 he Commitments\, a hit film about an Irish soul band\, and has since worke
 d with American blues and R&B stars Elvin Bishop\, Maria Muldaur\, Evelyn 
 Champagne King\, Michael Franti & Spearhead\, Zigaboo Modeliste (The Meter
 s)\, The Ray Charles Project\, and many more.\n​\nFlynn's new quartet DU
 BLINESQUE brings his deep soul and gospel roots together with the Irish mu
 sic traditions he was raised on.\n​\n"Dublinesque is my attempt to recre
 ate the kind of parties we had in my parent's house\, growing up in Dublin
 \," explains Flynn. "There'd be neighbours and friends and it would always
  end up as a sing-song/jam session. Everyone would participate - if you co
 uldn't hold a tune you'd perform a 'recitation' or tell a joke!\n​\n"The
 re was never any delineation between genres of music - whether it was Iris
 h tunes and ballads\, soul music or a Beatles song\," he emphasizes.\n​\
 nThe band brings together three talented Bay Area Irish traditional musici
 ans: fellow Irishman Félim Egan (The Black Brothers) on accordion\, local
  favorite Darcy Noonan on fiddle\, and from Basque country\, Spain\, Hecto
 r Bragado on banjo. They are also sometimes joined by special guests. Prev
 ious guests have included Glide Memorial Choir\, Maria Muldaur\, Mary Blac
 k\, Róisín O\, Michael Black\, Shay Black\, Autumn Rhodes\, Margaret Gra
 ham and dancers from the Kennelly\, Dillon and Whelan Schools of Irish Dan
 ce and the Cooley-Keegan Branch of Comhaltas Ceoltóirí.\n​\n"This is m
 y chance to play with some of my favorite musicians and recreate those par
 ties!" says Flynn.\n​\nFlynn's latest of three solo albums is 'Anywhere 
 But Home\,' celebrating Dublin from his San Francisco pandemic perspective
 . It received praise and widespread airplay in the US\, Canada\, Europe an
 d Australia.\n"Flynn's songwriting moves with true emotional register acro
 ss history\, folklore and poetry…with grit and true Dublin savvy.” Dei
 rdre Cronin - Irish Music Magazine
LOCATION:Occidental Center for the Arts\, 3850 Doris Murphy Court\, Occide
 ntal
URL:https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/dublinesque
 -album-release-party
X-SOURCE:Occidental Center for the Arts, Creative Sonoma, North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://creativesonoma.org/event/true-west/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:True West
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T203000
UID:260715FJptoGBaDkSc1K5kZP_-Zw
DESCRIPTION:Set in a suburban California home\, True West follows two brot
 hers with sharply contrasting personalities who reunite while house-sittin
 g for their mother. One is a disciplined\, aspiring screenwriter\, while t
 he other lives a more nomadic and unpredictable life. As they reconnect\, 
 their interactions shift from uneasy familiarity to intense competition\, 
 fueled by conflicting ambitions and long-standing tensions. Shepard's play
  delves into themes of authenticity\, creativity\, and the myth of the Ame
 rican frontier\, using sharp dialogue and dark humor to reveal the instabi
 lity beneath the surface of everyday life. As the brothers' dynamic evolve
 s\, the boundaries between their identities begin to blur\, raising questi
 ons about who they are and what defines them.
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/true-west/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
