BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "http://www.solanocollegetheatre.org/tickets"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:The Book of Will\, a dramatic comedy presented by Solano College T
 heatre
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T213000
UID:261023GbmOcPgcIUefcedkzn6u6g
DESCRIPTION:Solano College Theatre presents\n\nThe Book of Will\n\n📆Nov
 ember 6-22\, 2026\n\n📌4000 Suisun Valley Road\, Fairfield CA\n\n🎟 Ti
 ckets: www.solanocollegetheatre.org\n\n📞 \\(707\\) 864-7100\n\nWhere th
 ere’s a will\, there’s a way.\n\n“The Book of Will” brings to life
  the chaotic\, hilarious\, passionate\, and mostly true endeavor to compil
 e Shakespeare’s plays into the legendary First Folio!\n\nAbout the show:
  Without William Shakespeare\, we wouldn’t have literary masterpieces li
 ke “Romeo and Juliet.” But without Henry Condell and John Heminges\, w
 e would have lost half of Shakespeare’s plays forever! After the death o
 f their friend and mentor\, the two actors are determined to compile the F
 irst Folio and preserve the words that shaped their lives. They’ll just 
 have to borrow\, beg\, and band together to get it done. Amidst the noise 
 and color of Elizabethan London\, The Book of Will finds an unforgettable 
 true story of love\, loss\, and laughter\, and sheds new light on a man yo
 u may think you know.\n\nTickets $10-$25 online\, by phone\, or at the doo
 r!\n\nFri. 11/6 at 7:30 pm \\(opening night reception after the show!\\)\n
 \nSat. 11/7 at 7:30 pm \\(Enjoy our Old English Tap House - beer\, cider\,
  wine available for purchase\\)\n\nSun. 11/8 at 2 pm\n\nFri. 11/13 at 10 a
 m \\(Student Matinee\, all welcome!\\)\n\nFri. 11/13 at 7:30 pm \\(ASL Int
 erpretation provided!\\)\n\nSat. 11/14 at 7:30 pm \\(Enjoy our Old English
  Tap House - beer\, cider\, wine available for purchase\\)\n\nSun. 11/15 a
 t 2 pm\n\nThurs. 11/19 at 7:30 pm \\(Pay-what-you-WILL night!\\)\n\nFri. 1
 1/20 at 7:30 pm\n\nSat. 11/21 at 7:30 pm \\(Enjoy our Old English Tap Hous
 e - beer\, cider\, wine available for purchase\\)\n\nSun. 11/22 at 2 pm \\
 (closing show!\\)\n\nAbout the producer: Solano College Theatre is dedicat
 ed to providing quality theatre arts education to the next generation of t
 heatre professionals and producing shows that contribute meaningfully to t
 he culture and entertainment of our Solano County community.
LOCATION:Solano Col
URL:http://www.solanocollegetheatre.org/tickets
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://apocalypse.art/stimulant/", "Creative Sonoma": "https://creativesonoma.org/event/stimulant-art-as-remedy-for-diseased-culture-exhibition-events/", "Press Democrat": "https://apocalypse.art/stimulant/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://apocalypse.art/stimulant/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:STIMULANT: Art as Remedy for Diseased Culture\, Exhibition and Eve
 nts
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T220000
UID:261021BsaywvE-K02xqc33xM8_Pg
DESCRIPTION:In a diseased society with failing systems\, what can we do to
  turn things around? For two weeks a new exhibition from Sonoma County’s
  own Apocalypse Studio\, a father and daughter artist duo\, *STIMULANT: A
 rt as Remedy for Diseased Culture* proposes that art is the antidote and 
 creativity is the countermove. This exhibition explores the inner and oute
 r work of co-creating that antidote: art that stimulates society’s creat
 ivity - the social sculpture we all create together. There will be two per
 formances\, two lectures\, a Parisian -style Art Salon\, and times to visi
 t the large exhibition and talk with the artists. All events are free to 
 attend. Visit www.apocalypse.art/stimulant for details and schedule of eve
 nts.
LOCATION:Laguna Lab
URL:https://apocalypse.art/stimulant/
X-SOURCE:Creative Sonoma, North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.bandsintown.com/e/109008186?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=287&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Nancy Fawson Music
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T193000
UID:261016zEpxY5wpMEOr5UD98tZVHA
DESCRIPTION:Nancy Fawson is a powerhouse Bay Area-based vocalist and songw
 riter whose musical roots run deep in soul\, R&B and rock. Raised on the i
 conic sounds of Sam Cooke\, Etta James\, Aretha Franklin\, Chaka Khan\, St
 evie Wonder\, and Amy Winehouse\, Nancy’s musical influences have left a
 n indelible imprint on her voice and style. With a unique\, soulful tone a
 nd a passion for heartfelt expression\, Nancy connects with her audience o
 n a profound level—delivering each song with purity\, emotion\, and auth
 enticity.\n\nNancy’s vocal range spans across a variety of genres\, incl
 uding soul\, funk\, blues\, R&B\, and rock\, allowing her to bring versati
 lity to every performance. Whether performing with a duo or full band\, sh
 e engages audiences with her compelling stage presence and soulful deliver
 y.\n\nAs the lead singer of the popular Marin-based blues\, soul\, and fun
 k band Corner Pocket\, Nancy continues to captivate crowds with her raw en
 ergy and dedication to the craft. In addition to live performances\, she i
 s also available for recording session work\, offering her talents as both
  a lead and background vocalist.\n\nWith a sound that blends classic influ
 ences with modern flair\, Nancy Fawson is an artist whose voice you won’
 t soon forget.
LOCATION:Murphy's Irish Pub & Restaurant
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/109008186?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.bandsintown.com/e/109003039?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=287&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Illeagles
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T193000
UID:261012gqs4lxoemUKI5NNT5i5_bw
DESCRIPTION:What do people want when they go see a live band? The members 
 of SF Bay Area–based tribute band Illeagles believe audiences want to be
  fully engaged and captivated from the first note to the final encore. Aft
 er more than a year of sold-out performances\, that belief has proven true
  night after night. .\n\nIlleagles was founded in late 2016 when six frien
 ds came together with two things in common: a deep love for timeless West 
 Coast rock and a shared commitment to musical excellence. Each member is a
  standout musician in their own right\, and that collective passion led to
  countless hours of study\, rehearsal\, and refinement — carefully recre
 ating the signature harmonies\, soaring guitar lines\, and tight ensemble 
 interplay that defined a generation of classic American rock. From high-oc
 tane rock anthems to heartfelt\, harmony-driven ballads\, Illeagles delive
 rs a dynamic set that blends faithful musical craftsmanship with their own
  swagger\, energy\, and stage presence. It’s common for audiences to sta
 rt singing along from the very first song and keep going until the lights 
 come up — or their voices give out.
LOCATION:The California
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/109003039?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://raventheater.org/events/sweeney-todd/", "Press Democrat": "https://raventheater.org/events/sweeney-todd/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://raventheater.org/events/sweeney-todd/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Sweeney Todd
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T193000
UID:260909NeMFmOSoZ0OHmf7NW9_3ag
DESCRIPTION:Sweeney Todd is largely considered one of Stephen Sondheim’s
  masterpieces. With it\, he aimed to create a musical that could “scare 
 the hell out of everyone\,” and yet\, somehow\, be funny.\n\nThe story c
 enters around Sweeney Todd\, an unjustly exiled barber who returns to Lond
 on\, seeking vengeance against the lecherous judge who framed him and rava
 ged his young wife. The road to revenge leads Todd to Mrs. Lovett\, a reso
 urceful proprietress of a failing pie shop\, above which\, he opens a new 
 barber practice. Mrs. Lovett’s luck sharply shifts when Todd’s thirst 
 for blood inspires the integration of an ingredient into her meat pies tha
 t has the people of 19th Century London lining up…and the carnage has on
 ly just begun!\n\n\\***Content Advisory:** Adult language and violent the
 mes\, as well as controversial pie recipes. Recommended for 12+.\n\nRunnin
 g Time: 2 hours\, 40 minutes including one intermission.\n\nOctober 23rd\,
  24th\, 25th\, \\*29th\, 30th\, 31st\, Nov 1st\, 6th\, 7th\, 8th.\n\nBook 
 by Hugh Wheeler\n\nMusic and Lyrics by Stephen Sondheim\n\nDirected by Ste
 ven David Martin\n\n**Friday and Saturday Shows:** 7:30 PM\n\n**Sunday Mat
 inee:** 2:00 PM\n\n**\\*Value Thursday:** 7:30 PM\n\n**Admission:** \n\nA
