 e! This is an in-person symposium designed to provide cutting-edge insight
 s and practical strategies for managing diabetes across the care spectrum.
  This symposium features a wide range of expert-led presentations and case
  studies essential for clinicians looking to enhance their diabetes manage
 ment skills. You will have the opportunity to learn about: - Advancing Car
 e Through Technology Cases and a tech workshop that will allow you to get 
 hands-on experience with sensors\, pumps and early-stage type 1 diabetes s
 creening. - Lifestyle & Specialized Interventions Case studies and a culin
 ary workshop where you will actively build a healthy meal and learn tips y
 ou can share with your patients. - Technology and Lifestyle Medicine Eleva
 te your Practice with Expert-Led Lectures\, Interactive Workshops & Live C
 ooking Demos The day will culminate with a series of applied case presenta
 tions and Q&A with the experts\, offering a deep dive into real-world appl
 ications of the knowledge shared throughout the conference. This event is 
 ideal for all healthcare providers\, including physicians\, nurses\, pharm
 acists\, physician associates\, and CDCES\, involved in diabetes care and 
 management. Whether you’re in primary care\, endocrinology\, or any rela
 ted field\, this conference will equip you with the tools and knowledge yo
 u need to optimize patient outcomes. Don’t miss this opportunity to stay
