SUMMARY:Intermediate Salsa Class
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261110T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261110T193000
UID:2607046oAuYsuHaUmuOibTm3j0Dg
DESCRIPTION:This class is designed for dancers who have a solid grasp of t
 he basics and are eager to expand their repertoire with more complex and f
 luid movements.\n\nPre- requisite:\n\nSalsa Class Beginners\n\nEach week\,
  we’ll break down a new move\, focusing on the technique and connection 
 that will make you a more confident and stylish dancer. We’ll go beyond 
 the foundational steps to cover a wide range of essential intermediate pat
 terns and styling\, including:\n\nTurns and Spins:\n\nMaster your inside a
 nd outside turns\, double spins\, and the elegant 360 and Hand Toss moves.
 \n\nIntricate Patterns:\n\nLearn to execute the 360\, wrap\, as well as va
 rious Cross Body Lead variations like the U-Turn and Spiral.\n\nFootwork a
 nd Styling:\n\nEnhance your rhythm and flair with advanced footwork like t
 he Suzy Q\, Front Tap\, and Mambo Step. We’ll also work on styling with 
 a wrap and improving your posture and upper body movement.\n\nThis class i
 s your chance to refine your technique\, improve your lead-follow connecti
 on\, and add a variety of fun and dynamic moves to your salsa vocabulary. 
 Join us and elevate your dance!\n\nDetails:\n\nNo partner necessary — ro
 tations ensure everyone gets to dance.\n\nPlease wear non-marking shoe so
 les to protect the floor.\n\nArrive 10 minutes early to warm up and get s
 ettled.\n\nDate & Time: Tuesdays @ 6:30PM – 7:30PM
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/intermediate-salsa-clas
 s/17159571/2026-11-10T18
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.facebook.com/events/1317442349751921/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Poetry Book Club: If Not\, Winter: Fragments of Sappho by Sappho/A
 nne Carson
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261110T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261110T190000
UID:261009z93VVpYdXkuhLkJjZqwnaw
DESCRIPTION:Each month\, the Poetry Book Club meets online to discuss one 
 must-read book of poems\, whether a timeless classic or an award-winning c
 ontemporary. Led by Napa poet Kathleen Patterson\, who has been an enthusi
 astic book club member since its beginning\, meetings are open to all leve
 ls of poetry readers\, both the curious and the committed. ABOUT THE BOOK 
 In this "gorgeous translation" \\(The New York Times\\)\, one of our most 
 fearless and original poets provides a tantalizing window onto the genius 
 of a woman whose lyric power spans millennia. Of the nine books of lyrics 
 the ancient Greek poet Sappho is said to have composed\, only one poem has
  survived complete. The rest are fragments. In this miraculous new transla
 tion\, acclaimed poet and classicist Anne Carson presents all of Sappho’
 s fragments\, in Greek and in English\, as if on the ragged scraps of papy
 rus that preserve them\, inviting a thrill of discovery and conjecture tha
 t can be described only as electric—or\, to use Sappho’s words\, as 
 “thin fire ... racing under skin.” "Carson is in many ways \\[Sappho's
 \\] ideal translator.... Her command of language is hones to a perfect edg
 e and her approach to the text\, respectful yet imaginative\, results in v
 erse that lets Sappho shine forth." —Los Angeles Times ABOUT THE AUTHOR 
 ANNE CARSON was born in Canada and has been a professor of Classics for ov
 er thirty years. Her awards and honors include the Lannan Award\, the Push
 cart Prize\, the Griffin Trust Award for Excellence in Poetry\, and fellow
 ships from the Guggenheim and MacArthur Foundations.
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1317442349751921/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
