SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261031T052718Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T143000
SUMMARY:Whistler by Ann Patchett [OPTION 1]
DESCRIPTION:Novel Lovers of Sonoma County\, CA\n***Whistler*** by Ann Patc
 hett. If you rely on library copies\, reserve ASAP as there's a long wait 
 list. \\*\\**We're scheduling this book early in the month - 2nd and 3rd S
 at. - to avoid Thanksgiving weekend.\\*\\**\n\nPUBLISHER'S DESCRIPTION: "W
 hen Daphne Fuller and her husband Jonathan visit the Metropolitan Museum o
 f Art\, they notice an older\, white-haired gentleman following them. The 
 man turns out to be Eddie Triplett\, her former stepfather\, who had been 
 married to her mother for a little more than year when Daphne was nine. No
 w 53\, Daphne hasn’t seen Eddie for many years\, not since the fateful e
 vent that changed the direction of both their lives. Meeting again\, time 
 falls away\; while their relationship was brief\, it had a profound impact
  on them both\, and now that they are reunited\, they have no intention of
  ever being separated again.\n\n"*Whistler* is a story about two adults lo
 oking back over the choices they made\, and the choices that were made for
  them. It’s a story about bravery\, memory\, the often small yet consequ
 ential moments that define our lives\, and the endless stream of loss that
  in time comes for us all. Beautiful in its simplicity\, it is ultimately 
 about how love endures\, and how the feeling of being known by one other p
 erson\, even for a short period of time\, can change everything."\n\n"This
  exquisite writer has once again delivered an incandescent work of fiction
  — sweet\, but never sentimental\, infinitely wise and suffused with lov
 e. It’s also an ode to New York City itself…. While Patchett has clear
 ly drawn on actual events and individuals to produce this luminous work\, 
 she exhibits the expert novelist’s knack for following a plot where the 
 imagination takes it.... I didn't want it to end." - Leigh Haber\, ***The 
 Los Angeles Times***\n\n“Ann Patchett’s new novel is a rare phenomenon
  in contemporary fiction: a novel both majestic and intimate\, original an
 d masterful in its structure\, crystalline in its prose\, revelatory in it
 s insights\, utterly devastating yet ultimately uplifting in its emotional
  impact. . . . I think it is her best novel yet.” - Priscilla Gilman\, *
 **The Boston Globe***\n\n"Ann Patchett’s new novel\, *Whistler*\, is tha
 t loveliest of summer gifts\, a story of reconciliation\, of old affection
 s renewed\, of a family’s circumference enlarged. Fans of the author’s
  previous work will open these pages like an old shoebox of family photos.
  Newcomers — how I envy them those first moments — will discover a wri
 ter of gentle wit and quiet grace." - **Ron Charles**\n\n**Christine**: "J
 ust finished listening to this book and absolutely loved it! If you are in
 terested\, please listen to the Audible\, read by Patchett\, who is an exc
 ellent narrator. I've already recommended it to a number of friends. BIG t
 humbs' up! Would definitely read it again."\n\n**Nancy S**: "I liked *Whis
 tler* a lot. Mostly it hit some personal spots with characters just like p
 eople I know and situations I have been in. It is Anne Patchett in her mos
 t comfortable place— family type relationships\, reevaluated\, and trans
 formed and just about always for the better."
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/novel-lovers-of-sebastopol/events/316
 144717/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260816T190910Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260816T190910Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Occidental Center for the Arts": "https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/memoir-writing-workshop-for-women-crafting-your-life-story-pp3g6"}
X-SOURCE-ID:occidental_arts
SUMMARY:Memoir Writing Workshop for Women: Crafting Your Life Story
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T170000
UID:6acbf10873b3440700f08455@squarespace.com
DESCRIPTION:Transform Your Memories into Meaningful Narrative\nA Writing R
 etreat in Beautiful West County\nReady to tell your story? Your memories a
 re waiting to become literature.\nDiscover the power of your personal stor
 y and learn to craft it with authenticity\, depth\, and literary grace.\nW
 orkshop Overview\nJoin us for an immersive memoir writing experience desig
 ned to help you uncover\, shape\, and share the stories that have defined 
 your life. Whether you're a complete beginner or have been writing for yea
 rs\, this workshop will provide you with the tools and confidence to trans
 form your memories into compelling prose.\nWhat You will Learn:\nMemory Mi
 ning Techniques\n: Discover how to access and explore your most meaningful
  experiences\nNarrative Structure\n: Master the art of organizing your lif
 e events into engaging storylines\nVoice & Perspective\n: Develop your uni
 que authorial voice and choose the right point of view\nScene Construction
 \n: Learn to craft vivid\, cinematic scenes that bring your memories to li
 fe\nTruth vs. Accuracy\n: Navigate the ethical and creative considerations
  of memoir writing\nCharacter Development\n: Portray yourself and others w
 ith complexity and compassion\nRevision Strategies\n: Polish your work thr
 ough effective editing techniques\nWorkshop fee is $147\, $127 for OCA mem
 bers. This workshop is limited to 8 participants and will be held in the O
 CA Studio.\nRegister\nWorkshop Format\nDuration\n: One Saturday ( 4 hours 
 total).\nClass Size\n: Limited to 8 participants for personalized attentio
 n\nFormat\n: Interactive sessions combining instruction\, writing exercise
 s\, and peer feedback\nMaterials Provided\n: Writing prompts\, handouts\, 
 and recommended reading list\nWho Should Attend\nAspiring memoir writers a
 t any experience level\nAnyone interested in preserving family history\nWr
 iters looking to explore personal narrative\nIndividuals seeking therapeut
 ic writing experiences\nThose curious about the memoir genre\nWhat to Brin
 g\nNotebook and writing materials\nOpen mind and willingness to share (in 
 a supportive environment)\nNo previous writing experience necessary\nLed B
 y\nAlaura O’Dell MFA\, an experienced memoir author and writing instruct
 or\, will guide you through each step of the creative process with warmth\
 , expertise\, and encouragement. Alaura has guest lectured at Santa Rosa J
 unior College\, Marin College and Sonoma State University. O’Dell is cur
 rently working on a memoir\, which has attracted an international publishe
 r. For over 30 years she has lead women’s workshops and classes\, includ
 ing with her company\, Sacred Journeys for Women\, facilitating retreats t
 o sacred sites around the world.
LOCATION:Occidental Center for the Arts\, 3850 Doris Murphy Court\, Occide
 ntal
URL:https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/memoir-writ
 ing-workshop-for-women-crafting-your-life-story-pp3g6
X-SOURCE:Occidental Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
