DESCRIPTION:"Through portraiture\, we turn the camera toward dignity\, age
 ncy\, and self-representation. The women within these pages are dancers\, 
 artists\, beadworkers\, teachers\, mothers\, daughters\, grandmothers\, la
 nguage keepers\, and land and water defenders. They are culture bearers\, 
 but they are not defined by what they carry for others." — Julian Cook\,
  Co-CreatorThis project is funded by a grant from the Santa Rosa Junior Co
 llege Foundation Randolph Newman Cultural Enrichment Endowment.For more in
 formation\, visit the SRJC Multicultural Museum website. (https://museum.s
 antarosa.edu/event/standing-her-power-portraits-beyond-colonial-frame)
LAST-MODIFIED:20261008T192704Z
LOCATION:Multicultural Museum - Santa Rosa Campus
URL:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/event/23553-opening-reception-standing-
 in-her-power-portraits-beyo
