BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://creativesonoma.org/event/trio-da-paz/", "Creative Sonoma": "https://creativesonoma.org/event/trio-da-paz/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://creativesonoma.org/event/trio-da-paz/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Trio da Paz
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T190000
UID:260819kcl--0gROUOraI5g4gLPng
DESCRIPTION:Grammy-nominated Trio da Paz\, one of the most visible Brazili
 an jazz groups in the world featuring three of Brazil's most-in-demand mus
 icians: Romero Lubambo on guitar\, Nilson Matta on bass and Duduka da Fons
 eca on drums and percussion. They formed in 1986 and will be celebrating t
 heir 40th anniversary at THE 222 in an exclusive West Coast appearance. To
 gether\, Trio da Paz performs with a strong sense of cohesion\, bringing e
 nergy\, imagination\, and a deep musical connection to their work. The res
 ult is a trio that continues to create distinctive\, personal music\, blen
 ding Brazilian traditions with elements of modern jazz. Trio da Paz's soun
 d reflects a thoughtful integration of Brazilian musical styles and jazz i
 mprovisation\, drawing on the harmonies of bossa nova\, the rhythms of sam
 ba\, and the melodic intricacy of choro. Their acoustic trio format-guitar
 \, bass\, and drums-allows for close interaction among the musicians\, fos
 tering a conversational approach that highlights both rhythmic interplay a
 nd harmonic nuance. While grounded in tradition\, the group approaches fam
 iliar forms with flexibility\, allowing the music to evolve in unexpected 
 but natural directions. Each member\, established on the New York jazz sce
 ne as both a leader and collaborator\, contributes to a collective identit
 y shaped by original compositions alongside interpretations of Brazilian r
 epertoire.
LOCATION:D
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/trio-da-paz/
X-SOURCE:Creative Sonoma, North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108590341?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=287&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Andaz Hotel
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261114T190000
UID:261016SHyx6VWLuUSUZnN8XuTpWQ
DESCRIPTION:Callie Watts is a singer/songwriter from Northern California w
 ho was raised on classical music\, The Beatles and The Beach Boys before d
 iscovering Joni Mitchell\, Elton John\, Stevie Wonder\, Paul Simon\, Billy
  Joel\, Carole King\, and all the great writers of the ’60s and 70’s w
 ho have influenced her sound and writing style. After graduating high scho
 ol\, Callie began playing and performing solo\, as well as in local and ba
 y area bands of different genres. She’s played blues with Eric Lindell a
 nd the Reds\, funky soul with Phatty\, and jazz/swing with Savoy Swingers 
 along with many other various projects. Callie has taken turns throughout 
 her career as a keyboardist\, guitarist\, writer\, and lead/backing vocali
 st\, and she’s currently a member of the dynamic Sonoma County funk rock
  band Burrows and Dilbeck\, having joined in 2010 as part of the former ba
 nd Frobeck. Over time\, she’s had the honor of opening for acts such as 
 Bootsy Collins\, Elvin Bishop\, Huey Lewis and The News\, War\, Ozomatli\,
  Bill Champlin\, Booker T\, and the B52s. Callie continues to perform freq
 uently as an acoustic solo artist\, focusing on developing a core audience
  and a buzz for her original material. Come hang out and listen at venues 
 such as Aroma Roasters\, Rincon Valley Tap Room and Bottle Shop\, and Hopm
 onk Tavern.
LOCATION:Andaz Napa - A Concept By Hyatt
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108590341?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
