SUMMARY: Winsor & Newton Professional Watercolour Series - Class 3 of 3: 
 Lionfish
DESCRIPTION:Instructor: Ryan Martin\n\nDate: Monday\, November 16th\n\nTi
 me: 12:30PM-2PM\n\nLocation: Santa Rosa Store\n\nFree!\n\n\nClass 3 of 3:
  Lionfish — This is number three in a series of three classes using Winso
 r & Newton Professional Watercolour with artist Ryan Martin. Attend all t
 hree to learn week-by-week from Ryan but none are prerequisites if your s
 chedule does not allow. In this 90-minute session\, Ryan will guide you t
 hrough painting a detailed lionfish while learning how to use negative sp
 ace and Art Masking Fluid to preserve bright whites and create dramatic c
 ontrast. You’ll explore expressive brush strokes\, layered washes\, and c
 ontrolled color placement as you build the fish’s flowing fins\, stripes\
 , and patterns. Masking fluid will be used to save crisp highlights and d
 elicate details\, allowing the color and movement of the paint to shine. 
 This class focuses on seeing shapes\, protecting the white of the paper\,
  and letting watercolour create energy\, texture\, and life on the surfac
 e. All supplies are provided\, so you can try different pigments\, colors
 \, and brushes and discover what you enjoy using. Ryan will also be avail
 able after class to answer questions and help you choose materials to kee
 p exploring at home.\n\n\nLimited seats available—reserve your spot today
 !\n\n\nRyan Martin lives and works in the San Francisco Bay Area where he
  attended the California College of the Arts. Through painting and drawin
 g\, Martin creates surreal\, dream-like compositions of his subjects. He 
 is influenced by his Native American (Mexican/Seri) and Russian heritage 
 through painting reinterpretations of war bonnets and kokoshniks haloing 
 his subjects. Martin’s artwork has been highlighted by numerous media inc
 luding The Advocate\, Creative Boom\, The Art of Man and others. He has e
 xhibited widely across the United States\, including the deYoung Museum\,
  Mark Wolfe Contemporary\, Modern Eden Gallery of San Francisco\, Elizabe
 th Houston Gallery of NYC\, as well as numerous fairs including SCOPE\, U
 ntitled Art in Miami and Volta NY.\n\nWebsite: ryanmartinart.com http://r
 yanmartinart.com • Instagram: @ryanmartinart
CATEGORIES:Santa-Rosa,Watercolor,Free-Demo
