UID:26070510x4dimBK0mENVQZkuqltg
DESCRIPTION:Ready to dance? Join our beginner salsa class where no experie
 nce or partner is needed. Just comfortable shoes and desire to have fun!\n
 \nGreat for first timers!\n\nNo dance experience required\n\nNon-marking s
 hoes soles\n\nNo partner necessary\n\nOur relaxed environment is perfect f
 or learning salsa basics\, as we make it fun and enjoyable. In this class 
 you will learn basic directional steps\, proper frame for partner-work and
  simple turn patterns. We organize our curriculum so that the movements ar
 e easy to remember. Join us to learn the fundamentals! No experience is ne
 cessary and no partner is required. Drop-in fee is $20.\n\nDate & Time: Tu
 esdays @ 5:30PM – 6:30PM\n\nAddress: 4140 Redwood Highway \\#8 San Rafae
 l\, CA\n\nNote: Arrive 10 minutes before. No floor marking shoe soles allo
 wed.
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/beginner-salsa-tuesdays
 /17157360/2026-11-17T17
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://solanolibrary.libnet.info/event/17551235"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Beginner Friendly Sewing Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261117T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261117T193000
UID:261028IQWjLTW2lki4WoKa5IXOlQ
DESCRIPTION:The Vallejo John F. Kennedy is hosting a start-to-finish guide
 d sewing program making an electric heating pad cover. To make our covers 
 we will be using an old flannel sheet. We will provide one fabric option\,
  but you are more than welcome to bring your own materials if you have any
  you would prefer to use. If you bring your own fabric\, please make sure 
 it is a stable woven. We recommend flannels \\(like an old flannel shirt\,
  pajama bottoms\, or a pillow case\\) for cozier experience when using the
  heating pads\, but quilting cottons and linens would work as well. We hav
 e 5 sewing machines available for the workshop. If you have your own machi
 ne you would like to bring\, please let us so know so we can set up the ro
 om accordingly. If you have any questions\, please call the library: \\(86
 6\\) 572-7587. Due to limited machinery and supplies\, we require registra
 tion for this event. Although this program is offered on the 3rd and the 1
 7th\, this is a standalone workshop that will be done in one session. Supp
 lies: We will provide all materials\, however you are welcome to bring you
 r own fabric and thread if you prefer. For this project you will need: One
  electric heating pad \\(not provided\\) One piece of fabric that is sligh
 tly bigger than the heating pad when folded in half. Alternatively\, if yo
 u have old flannel clothes that you can upcycle\, you can use that instead
 .
LOCATION:Vallejo John F. Kennedy Library
URL:https://solanolibrary.libnet.info/event/17551235
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
