 rev.1789492221.jpg
CATEGORIES:Museum
DESCRIPTION:"Through portraiture\, we turn the camera toward dignity\, age
 ncy\, and self-representation. The women within these pages are dancers\, 
 artists\, bead workers\, teachers\, mothers\, daughters\, grandmothers\, l
 anguage keepers\, and land and water defenders. They are culture bearers\,
  but they are not defined by what they carry for others." — Julian Cook\
 , Co-Creator  A Portrait Series by Alexa LexMex Treviño (https://www.lexm
 exart.com/about) in collaboration with the SRJC Multicultural Museum.This 
 exhibit is funded by a grant from the Santa Rosa Junior College Foundation
  Randolph Newman Cultural Enrichment Endowment.For more information\, visi
 t the SRJC Multicultural Museum website. (https://museum.santarosa.edu/eve
 nt/standing-her-power-portraits-beyond-colonial-frame)
LAST-MODIFIED:20261008T193338Z
LOCATION:Multicultural Museum - Santa Rosa Campus
URL:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/event/23769-standing-in-her-power-portr
 aits-beyond-the-colonial-fr
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  "Through portraiture\, we turn the camer
 a toward dignity\, agency\, and self-representation. The women within thes
 e pages are dancers\, artists\, bead workers\, teachers\, mothers\, daught
 ers\, grandmothers\, language keepers\, and land and water defenders. They
  are culture bearers\, but they are not defined by what they carry for oth
 ers." — Julian Cook\, Co-Creator</p><p>  A Portrait Series by <a href="h
 ttps://www.lexmexart.com/about" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Alexa LexMe
 x Treviño</a> in collaboration with the SRJC Multicultural Museum.</p><p>
 <em>This exhibit is funded by a grant from the Santa Rosa Junior College F
 oundation Randolph Newman Cultural Enrichment Endowment.</em></p><p><a hre
 f="https://museum.santarosa.edu/event/standing-her-power-portraits-beyond-
 colonial-frame" target="_blank" rel="noopener">For more information\, visi
 t the SRJC Multicultural Museum website.</a></p>
