DESCRIPTION:**Singles Bingo + Switch | Bingo with a Touch of Speed Dating*
 *\n\nSick of Dating Apps?\n\nJoin Catch Singles and North Bay Bingo for a 
 fun\, interactive evening at Trailhouse Café in Santa Rosa. We’re putti
 ng a fresh spin on traditional speed dating by combining bingo\, rotating 
 seats\, and plenty of opportunities to connect.\n\nAs bingo rounds end\, p
 articipants switch seats\, giving everyone a chance to meet new people nat
 urally. No awkward interviews or forced conversations — just good compan
 y\, a little friendly competition\, and the possibility of meeting someone
  special.\n\nAfter bingo\, stick around for a relaxed social mixer to cont
 inue conversations and make new connections!\n\n**Thursday\, November 19 |
  7:00–9:30 PM** (check in 6:45) Trailhouse Café | Santa Rosa Singles ag
 es 30–49 $40 per person | Includes one beverage\n\nLimited spots availab
 le. Advance registration required.\n\n**Hosted by Catch Singles — Bringi
 ng local singles together\, one event at a time.**
LOCATION:Trailhouse 
URL:https://c33ab2fd-1a51-41cb-998d-23ec1d275308.paylinks.godaddy.com/e4a1
 bf9d-038f-4da5-a90a-6ff
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "http://www.petalumareaderstheatre.com"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Pet the Elephant
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261119T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261119T210000
UID:261015WLFiLAVdbUuRC-ZK8k9EdA
DESCRIPTION:Nov 19-20\, 7pm and Nov 21\, 2pm\n\nSo you think your family i
 s crazy around the holidays?\n\nWait till you meet the Naybors!\n\nIt's th
 e mid 1980's\, at 4AM on Thanksgiving Day and the scrumptious dinner is fa
 st approaching.\n\nTime is limited.\n\nThe task is gargantuan.\n\nEva's st
 ruggling to keep her secret hidden at all costs. But she can feel the madn
 ess starting to crack through her controlled veneer.\n\nAs if all that isn
 't enough\, Angel\, the eldest daughter refuses to come home today\, of al
 l days. Mikey\, the middle child\, is snarky about being disconnected from
  his phone. Wouldn't you know it\, Deborah\, the baby of the family\, is o
 ut way too late with that boy. Aunt Ruth is still eavesdropping on private
  discussions. And Sam\, Eve's long-suffering husband has terrifying memori
 es surfacing\, again.\n\nWanna bet they don't even make it to the appetize
 rs?
LOCATION:Mercury Theater
URL:http://www.petalumareaderstheatre.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
