DESCRIPTION:As generative AI becomes embedded across disciplines\, higher 
 education faces a pivotal moment—not of battle between opposing camps\, 
 but of intentional design.  Generative systems offer novel capabilities fo
 r research\, creation\, and learning\, yet their ultimate value depends en
 tirely on how thoughtfully we guide them.Neha Saigal is building AI-native
  learning tools grounded in how kids are actually wired to learn.Learn mor
 e on the SRJC Computer Studies' AI Talks website. (https://cs.santarosa.ed
 u/ai-talks-2026)
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T190629Z
LOCATION:Online
URL:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/event/23947-neha-saigal-human-agency-ma
 chine-inquiry
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  As generative AI becomes embedded across
  disciplines\, higher education faces a pivotal moment—not of battle bet
 ween opposing camps\, but of intentional design.</p><p>  Generative system
 s offer novel capabilities for research\, creation\, and learning\, yet th
 eir ultimate value depends entirely on how thoughtfully we guide them.</p>
 <p><strong>Neha Saigal</strong> is building AI-native learning tools groun
 ded in how kids are actually wired to learn.</p><p><a href="https://cs.san
 tarosa.edu/ai-talks-2026" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Learn more on the
  SRJC Computer Studies' AI Talks website.</a></p>
