BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "http://www.solanocollegetheatre.org/tickets"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:The Book of Will\, a dramatic comedy presented by Solano College T
 heatre
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T220000
UID:261023o1KZb1uJtEO-XlpUyuy7Ug
DESCRIPTION:Solano College Theatre presents\n\nThe Book of Will\n\n📆Nov
 ember 6-22\, 2026\n\n📌4000 Suisun Valley Road\, Fairfield CA\n\n🎟 Ti
 ckets: www.solanocollegetheatre.org\n\n📞 \\(707\\) 864-7100\n\nWhere th
 ere’s a will\, there’s a way.\n\n“The Book of Will” brings to life
  the chaotic\, hilarious\, passionate\, and mostly true endeavor to compil
 e Shakespeare’s plays into the legendary First Folio!\n\nAbout the show:
  Without William Shakespeare\, we wouldn’t have literary masterpieces li
 ke “Romeo and Juliet.” But without Henry Condell and John Heminges\, w
 e would have lost half of Shakespeare’s plays forever! After the death o
 f their friend and mentor\, the two actors are determined to compile the F
 irst Folio and preserve the words that shaped their lives. They’ll just 
 have to borrow\, beg\, and band together to get it done. Amidst the noise 
 and color of Elizabethan London\, The Book of Will finds an unforgettable 
 true story of love\, loss\, and laughter\, and sheds new light on a man yo
 u may think you know.\n\nTickets $10-$25 online\, by phone\, or at the doo
 r!\n\nFri. 11/6 at 7:30 pm \\(opening night reception after the show!\\)\n
 \nSat. 11/7 at 7:30 pm \\(Enjoy our Old English Tap House - beer\, cider\,
  wine available for purchase\\)\n\nSun. 11/8 at 2 pm\n\nFri. 11/13 at 10 a
 m \\(Student Matinee\, all welcome!\\)\n\nFri. 11/13 at 7:30 pm \\(ASL Int
 erpretation provided!\\)\n\nSat. 11/14 at 7:30 pm \\(Enjoy our Old English
  Tap House - beer\, cider\, wine available for purchase\\)\n\nSun. 11/15 a
 t 2 pm\n\nThurs. 11/19 at 7:30 pm \\(Pay-what-you-WILL night!\\)\n\nFri. 1
 1/20 at 7:30 pm\n\nSat. 11/21 at 7:30 pm \\(Enjoy our Old English Tap Hous
 e - beer\, cider\, wine available for purchase\\)\n\nSun. 11/22 at 2 pm \\
 (closing show!\\)\n\nAbout the producer: Solano College Theatre is dedicat
 ed to providing quality theatre arts education to the next generation of t
 heatre professionals and producing shows that contribute meaningfully to t
 he culture and entertainment of our Solano County community.
LOCATION:Solano Col
URL:http://www.solanocollegetheatre.org/tickets
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://music.sonoma.edu/events/symphony-orchestra-2?utm_source=sonoma_calendars&utm_medium=event_calendar&utm_campaign=fall_2026_symphony_orchestra_nov20", "Creative Sonoma": "https://creativesonoma.org/event/symphony-orchestra/", "Press Democrat": "https://music.sonoma.edu/events/symphony-orchestra-2?utm_source=sonoma_calendars&utm_medium=event_calendar&utm_campaign=fall_2026_symphony_orchestra_nov20"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://music.sonoma.edu/events/symphony-orchestra-2?utm_source=sonoma_calendars&utm_medium=event_calendar&utm_campaign=fall_2026_symphony_orchestra_nov20"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Symphony Orchestra
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261120T193000
UID:261031JidpFAZJREmrd89mslQmZw
DESCRIPTION:C Major Moods\n\nJoint Concert featuring the Sonoma State Symp
 hony Orchestra \\(Alexander Kahn\, Music Director\\) and the Santa Rosa Sy
 mphony Young People's Chamber Orchestra\\(Aaron Westman\, Music Director\\
 )\n\nPlease join us for an evening of two remarkable symphonies from the e
 arly nineteenth century\, both of which are in the key of C!\n\nThis conce
 rt is a collaboration between the Sonoma State Symphony Orchestra and the 
 Santa Rosa Symphony Young People's Chamber Orchestra\, who will join force
 s throughout the program.\n\nOn the first half of the program is the passi
 onate and virtuousic Symphony no. 1 from 1847 by Emile Mayer\, the most pr
 olific female composer active in Germany during the 19th century. After th
 e intermission we bring you Beethoven's ground-breaking Symphony No. 1 \\(
 1800\\)\, the symphony that launched the Romantic period and put Beethoven
 's name on the map as a symphonist. The Beethoven will be performed withou
 t a conductor\, led from the violin by SSU violin/viola faculty member and
  YPCO Music Director Aaron Westman.
LOCATION:Green Music Center - Weill Hall
URL:https://music.sonoma.edu/events/symphony-orchestra-2?utm_source=sonoma
 _calendars&utm_medium=event_calendar&utm_campaign=fall_2026_symphony_orche
 stra_nov20
X-SOURCE:Creative Sonoma, North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
