BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://jarvisconservatory.ticketspice.com/primavera", "Press Democrat": "https://jarvisconservatory.ticketspice.com/primavera"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://jarvisconservatory.ticketspice.com/primavera"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:International Film:  PRIMAVERA
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T180000
UID:2609298sqFhP-Lu0KFStXoAIdAyw
DESCRIPTION:Music and power intertwine in Primavera\, as Antonio Vivaldi t
 eaches an orphan how to imagine a new destiny for herself.\n\nA talented v
 iolinist\, Cecilia\, confined in an orphanage\, meets Vivaldi who becomes 
 her teacher. Under his mentorship and through his music\, she gains courag
 e to break free from the life she was destined for and pursue her passion.
 \n\nVenice\, early 18th century. Renowned for its exceptional music progra
 m\, the Pièta orphanage is home to Cecilia\, a 20-year-old violin virtuos
 o. Despite her extraordinary talent\, Cecilia remains confined within the 
 orphanage and like all the girls there\, her only escape seems to get marr
 ied. Yet\, her life changes drastically when Antonio Vivaldi\, a brilliant
  and ambitious composer\, arrives as the new violin teacher. Through a com
 plex artistic relationship with Vivaldi and his music\, Cecilia finds the 
 strength to challenge the destiny that once seemed inevitable.
LOCATION:Jarvis Conservatory
URL:https://jarvisconservatory.ticketspice.com/primavera
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
