SUMMARY:Pi Jacobs\, Ben Musser & Walker Young at The Lost Church Santa Ros
 a
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T223000
UID:261028A_k5Q7szLEeunt7ApzQCPw
DESCRIPTION:**Pi Jacobs** draws inspiration from her unconventional upbrin
 ging in Northern California\, where she was raised by “radical hippies\,
  bohemians and nerds”.   She is signed to LA’s Blackbird Record Label
 \, and her 2024 album\, “Soldier On”\, was on the Americana Music Asso
 ciation Chart top 50 upon release in 2024\, and stayed there for over 16 w
 eeks.  \n\nPi has released two new topical singles in 2026. Mrs. Nobody\,
  a powerful ballad with references to to the SAVES act\, limiting married 
 women’s right to vote\, and Nogales\, a song chronicling racial profilin
 g at the Mexican-American  border\, via a personal experience. “I was h
 aving trouble writing\, until I started writing about it head on”. The s
 inger-songwriter states\, with regards to the political nature of her new 
 music.  She is currently recording her next album\, which will include No
 gales\, Mrs. Nobody\, and other songs that reflect on the current experien
 ce of living in the US.  Nogales has been receiving airplay on Sirius XM\
 , The Village\, as of July 2026\n\nhttps://PiJacobs.com  https://Facebook
 .com/PiJacobsMusic      https://Instagram.com/PiJacobs    https://www
 .youtube.com/PiJacobsMusic\n\n**Ben Musser & Walker Young** make up a root
 s power-duo from Jackson Hole\, Wyoming who perform vocally driven soul an
 d country music. Young (of Truth & Salvage Co.) performs accordion\, keybo
 ards and vocals and Musser (formerly Benyaro) performs guitars\, drums\, a
 nd vocals. The duo is promoting Musser’s new solo album ‘Sentimental F
 ever’ (Blackbird Record Label) that's been featured on CMT\, NPR\, EARMI
 LK\, Visual Atelier 8\, and receiving AAA radio play across the country. M
 usser and Young are currently recording their premiere EP at Musser's stud
 io in Jackson Hole. Passionate performances\, boot-stomping joy\, and seas
 oned vocals that move both themselves and others to sing and feel the emot
 ion\, explain the Ben Musser & Walker Young live music performance experie
 nce. https://www.instagram.com/benmussermusichttps://www.facebook.com/ben
 mussermusicahttps://www.tiktok.com/@benmussermusic
LOCATION:The Lost Church
URL:https://thelostchurch.my.salesforce-sites.com/ticket/#/instances/a0FUh
 00000DV2CXMA1
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "http://www.solanocollegetheatre.org/tickets"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:The Book of Will\, a dramatic comedy presented by Solano College T
 heatre
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T220000
UID:261023F5pWTcLCD0yYzdD4-W3Ggw
DESCRIPTION:Solano College Theatre presents\n\nThe Book of Will\n\n📆Nov
 ember 6-22\, 2026\n\n📌4000 Suisun Valley Road\, Fairfield CA\n\n🎟 Ti
 ckets: www.solanocollegetheatre.org\n\n📞 \\(707\\) 864-7100\n\nWhere th
 ere’s a will\, there’s a way.\n\n“The Book of Will” brings to life
  the chaotic\, hilarious\, passionate\, and mostly true endeavor to compil
 e Shakespeare’s plays into the legendary First Folio!\n\nAbout the show:
  Without William Shakespeare\, we wouldn’t have literary masterpieces li
 ke “Romeo and Juliet.” But without Henry Condell and John Heminges\, w
 e would have lost half of Shakespeare’s plays forever! After the death o
 f their friend and mentor\, the two actors are determined to compile the F
 irst Folio and preserve the words that shaped their lives. They’ll just 
 have to borrow\, beg\, and band together to get it done. Amidst the noise 
 and color of Elizabethan London\, The Book of Will finds an unforgettable 
 true story of love\, loss\, and laughter\, and sheds new light on a man yo
 u may think you know.\n\nTickets $10-$25 online\, by phone\, or at the doo
 r!\n\nFri. 11/6 at 7:30 pm \\(opening night reception after the show!\\)\n
 \nSat. 11/7 at 7:30 pm \\(Enjoy our Old English Tap House - beer\, cider\,
  wine available for purchase\\)\n\nSun. 11/8 at 2 pm\n\nFri. 11/13 at 10 a
 m \\(Student Matinee\, all welcome!\\)\n\nFri. 11/13 at 7:30 pm \\(ASL Int
 erpretation provided!\\)\n\nSat. 11/14 at 7:30 pm \\(Enjoy our Old English
  Tap House - beer\, cider\, wine available for purchase\\)\n\nSun. 11/15 a
 t 2 pm\n\nThurs. 11/19 at 7:30 pm \\(Pay-what-you-WILL night!\\)\n\nFri. 1
 1/20 at 7:30 pm\n\nSat. 11/21 at 7:30 pm \\(Enjoy our Old English Tap Hous
 e - beer\, cider\, wine available for purchase\\)\n\nSun. 11/22 at 2 pm \\
 (closing show!\\)\n\nAbout the producer: Solano College Theatre is dedicat
 ed to providing quality theatre arts education to the next generation of t
 heatre professionals and producing shows that contribute meaningfully to t
 he culture and entertainment of our Solano County community.
LOCATION:Solano Col
URL:http://www.solanocollegetheatre.org/tickets
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
