DESCRIPTION:2026 marks the 110th anniversary of Jack London’s death. Vol
 unteer Park Historian\, Lou Leal will preside over the service.  Songwrit
 er and vocalist\, Jeff Falconer will perform his original song written in 
 memory of Jack London. Jack London died of kidney failure on November 22\,
  1916. In his short life he accomplished much\, not only as a writer of fi
 fty books\, but also as an adventurer\, reporter\, war correspondent\, spo
 rts article writer\, and innovative farmer. He was in the process of devel
 oping 
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park\, 2400 London Ranch Road\, Glen E
 llen\, CA 95442
