BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "http://www.solanocollegetheatre.org/tickets"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:The Book of Will\, a dramatic comedy presented by Solano College T
 heatre
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T160000
UID:261023zzOh-NBJo0mwjyb6r8F-Ag
DESCRIPTION:Solano College Theatre presents\n\nThe Book of Will\n\n📆Nov
 ember 6-22\, 2026\n\n📌4000 Suisun Valley Road\, Fairfield CA\n\n🎟 Ti
 ckets: www.solanocollegetheatre.org\n\n📞 \\(707\\) 864-7100\n\nWhere th
 ere’s a will\, there’s a way.\n\n“The Book of Will” brings to life
  the chaotic\, hilarious\, passionate\, and mostly true endeavor to compil
 e Shakespeare’s plays into the legendary First Folio!\n\nAbout the show:
  Without William Shakespeare\, we wouldn’t have literary masterpieces li
 ke “Romeo and Juliet.” But without Henry Condell and John Heminges\, w
 e would have lost half of Shakespeare’s plays forever! After the death o
 f their friend and mentor\, the two actors are determined to compile the F
 irst Folio and preserve the words that shaped their lives. They’ll just 
 have to borrow\, beg\, and band together to get it done. Amidst the noise 
 and color of Elizabethan London\, The Book of Will finds an unforgettable 
 true story of love\, loss\, and laughter\, and sheds new light on a man yo
 u may think you know.\n\nTickets $10-$25 online\, by phone\, or at the doo
 r!\n\nFri. 11/6 at 7:30 pm \\(opening night reception after the show!\\)\n
 \nSat. 11/7 at 7:30 pm \\(Enjoy our Old English Tap House - beer\, cider\,
  wine available for purchase\\)\n\nSun. 11/8 at 2 pm\n\nFri. 11/13 at 10 a
 m \\(Student Matinee\, all welcome!\\)\n\nFri. 11/13 at 7:30 pm \\(ASL Int
 erpretation provided!\\)\n\nSat. 11/14 at 7:30 pm \\(Enjoy our Old English
  Tap House - beer\, cider\, wine available for purchase\\)\n\nSun. 11/15 a
 t 2 pm\n\nThurs. 11/19 at 7:30 pm \\(Pay-what-you-WILL night!\\)\n\nFri. 1
 1/20 at 7:30 pm\n\nSat. 11/21 at 7:30 pm \\(Enjoy our Old English Tap Hous
 e - beer\, cider\, wine available for purchase\\)\n\nSun. 11/22 at 2 pm \\
 (closing show!\\)\n\nAbout the producer: Solano College Theatre is dedicat
 ed to providing quality theatre arts education to the next generation of t
 heatre professionals and producing shows that contribute meaningfully to t
 he culture and entertainment of our Solano County community.
LOCATION:Solano Col
URL:http://www.solanocollegetheatre.org/tickets
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://srjc.universitytickets.com/", "Press Democrat": "https://srjc.universitytickets.com/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://srjc.universitytickets.com/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Disney's Frozen the Broadway Musical
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T162000
UID:261022XDcn0Q1zOUihLXPqmfRTog
DESCRIPTION:*Disney's Frozen The Broadway Musical* is based on the 2013 Di
 sney animated film\, focusing on the estranged relationship between royal 
 sisters Elsa and Anna. When Elsa loses control of her ice powers the kingd
 om is plunged into eternal winter\, Elsa flees\, and Anna embarks on a jou
 rney with Kristoff\, Sven\, and Olaf to find her sister and heal the kingd
 om.\n\nBook by Jennifer Lee\n\nMusic and Lyrics by Kristen Anderson-Lopez 
 and Robert Lopez\n\nDirected by Sarah Wintermeyer\n\nMusic and Vocal Direc
 tion by Gordon Pyle\n\nChoreography by Jolene Johnson
LOCATION:SRJC Burbank Auditorium
URL:https://srjc.universitytickets.com/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://performingartsnapavalley.org/nvc-chorale-fall-26/", "Press Democrat": "https://performingartsnapavalley.org/nvc-chorale-fall-26/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://performingartsnapavalley.org/nvc-chorale-fall-26/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Napa Valley College Chorale - "A Hero's Journey"
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261122T151500
UID:261013dOiLv_sCSUiCNgbvURxskg
DESCRIPTION:Every story worth telling begins the same way. Not with a plan
 . Not with a hero who is ready. \n\nIt begins with a call. \n\nJoseph Ca
 mpbell found the same journey running beneath human stories across every c
 ulture and every century: the ordinary life disrupted\, the threshold cros
 sed\, the road that takes everything\, the transformation that finally mak
 es the return possible. \n\n*A Hero’s Journey* is a choral concert bui
 lt on that arc. Five movements. One story. Music spanning Vivaldi to Rodge
 rs and Hammerstein\, a forgotten inscription on a cellar wall in wartime C
 ologne\, a Broadway meditation on hope written for a daughter\, ancient li
 turgy\, and a 21st-century voice asking\, quietly\, what it costs to get d
 ressed and show up. Between movements\, students from the NVC Reader’s T
 heater class give voice to the arc — narrating the journey from call to 
 return. \n\nThe NVC Chorale invites you to make the journey with them —
  a concert about the rest of us. The ones who weren’t ready. The ones 
 who went anyway.
LOCATION:Napa Valley College Performing Arts Center
URL:https://performingartsnapavalley.org/nvc-chorale-fall-26/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
