DESCRIPTION:Tuesday\, November 24\, 2026\n\n6:00pm    Doors open 5:30 pm
 \n\nFree entry. Donations greatly appreciated.\n\nConcessions open for pur
 chase.\n\nAssistive listening devices available.\n\n Sponsored by Jim & C
 arol Dvorak\n\nMortimer Brewster\, a writer known for his dislike of marri
 age\, surprises everyone by falling for his neighbor Elaine Harper. They g
 et married on Halloween. When they go home to share the news\, Mortimer di
 scovers a body hidden in a window seat. As he deals with his quirky aunts\
 , troubled uncle\, and dangerous brother\, he realizes his family is even 
 more unusual than he imagined.\n\nReleased Sep 23\, 1944\n\nComedy\n\nRunt
 ime 1h 58m
